\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 DONIE O'SULLIVAN, CNN CORRESPONDENT: Yes. So, this was a very long essay he wrote last night on the platform. So, this is by far the most laughable claim. They are cherry-picking what research they release. The most obvious example of that came just a few weeks ago. Facebook put out a report about the most popular links on its platform in the second quarter of this year. An executive at the time had they brought it out said this makes us probably the most transparent platform on the internet. That report was for the second quarter.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 What happened a few days later, we found out there was an actual report for the first quarter of this year but they shelved it because it made them look bad, because the top link on the platform was a piece of anti-vaccine misinformation. So, they are cherry-picking their research and now they're telling us that we are supposed believe them, take them at their word about their research.}
